  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Danish Consortium Project on Survivor Recovery, Human Rights and Independent Media in Post-July Uprising Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the development cooperation among the parties is &#x2018;Promoting an 
inclusive, resilience-promoOng transition to democracy and human rights in Bangladesh&#x2019;. 

Key results:
&#x2022;	By 2028, civil society organisations have enhanced capacity to deliver and promote access to trauma-informed, survivor-centred rehabilitation and other forms of redress for survivors of torture and related violations perpetrated in context of the July 2024 Uprising in Bangladesh
&#x2022;	Human rights actors (including the NHRC and CSOs) undertake strong advocacy for a revision of the NHRC legal framework, to enable an NHRI with a strong mandate and alignment with the Paris Principles, and human rights actors articulate demands for human rights accountability and promote a sustained vision for human rights-based reform.
&#x2022;	A pluralistic, inclusive and resilient media environment in Bangladesh, strengthened through reform processes, safety mechanisms, and strategic support to an emerging independent media sector</narrative>
  </description>
